            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AUTUMNFIRE71"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are terrific! My daughters loved them and called them \"banana fries\".\nI have never used plantains before. They are difficult to peel but I figured out a good way. Cut the end off and slice down the length of the plantain. Then peel the cut edges apart.\nFor this recipe it says gather about two tablespoons together...Squish them together into a little ball. They will stick together and still make the 'legs' of the aranita.\nFast and easy!",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-15T18:46:45.213Z"
          }
